<Solution>

  <!-- Every project, so that the one documented build command builds all of them.

       Without this file "dotnet build" at the repo root resolved to the single csproj
       beside it, which is the old WPF window, and XzoundUI and XzoundCli were never
       built at all. That is not a tidiness problem: both window heads emit an assembly
       named XzoundWave, so the newest XzoundWave.exe in the tree was the WPF one, and
       anybody who built and then ran what they had just built was running the other
       window and wondering why their change had not appeared. It cost a real afternoon.

       XzoundWave.csproj, the WPF window, stays in the list because it is what the root
       build has always produced and dropping it here would silently stop producing it.
       It is reference only now; XzoundUI is the window under development. -->

  <Project Path="XzoundCore/XzoundCore.csproj" />
  <Project Path="XzoundLogic/XzoundLogic.csproj" />
  <Project Path="XzoundCli/XzoundCli.csproj" />
  <Project Path="XzoundUI/XzoundUI.csproj" />
  <Project Path="XzoundWave.csproj" />

</Solution>
